ruling a kingdom is hard work and if you  don't know what you're doing your noble  crusade to unite the realms might end a  bit early here's some tips that will get  you started in the colorful world of  ninokuni - number one be well equipped  for most RPGs this goes without saying  however in ninokuni two weapons armors  and charms drop at a staggering rate and  because each party member can carry  three weapons at a time things can get  overwhelming fortunately the game  automatically sorts your best weapons  and armor to the top so every now and  then just hop in to the skills and  equipment screen and look for the ones  on HIGH easy number to manage your  metres during your battles you've  probably noticed the numbers on the left  of the screen  these are Xing gauges as you fight with  your equipped weapon this gauge will  build up and when it reaches a hundred  percent you can unleash a more powerful  version of a skill in order to get the  most out of the Zeen gauge I would  recommend using manual weapon switching  rather than automatic or semi-automatic  number three don't ignore side quests  and ninokuni - most side quests net you  more than just cash and experience some  of them allow you to recruit new  citizens for your expanding Kingdom  while building your castle may not have  any obvious benefits at the get-go it  becomes imperative later on if you see  this little human-like symbol next to a  quest it means you'll get a new citizen  upon completion you should make it a  point to complete as many of these  quests as you can also make sure to  revisit towns you've already been to to  see if new quests are available check  swift solutions regularly will come to  swift solutions if you are short a  citizen or need someone with a specific  skill head over to swift solutions you  should be able to find one of these guys  at every major city in the game  so if solutions allows you to take on  simple quests in exchange for tokens of  gratitude you can use these tokens to  recruit new citizens for your kingdom or  purchase rare items number five don't  ignore the tactic tweeker the tactic  Tweaker allows you to mess around with  some simple but powerful combat  parameters as you progress you'll learn  battle points which allow you to level  up these four sections  stro finna tease elements in ailments  spoils and arts of war  once you've leveled these up a few times  you can start playing with these  settings I would recommend investing in  spoils so you can adjust how much  experience and loot you get after a  battle  [Music]  but beware if you set it so you earn  more experienced enemies won't drop as  much money you can save yourself a lot  of grinding and resource gathering if  you tweak these settings early on the  arts of war setting also allows you to  boost the effectiveness of your dodge  and block which depending on what you're  up against  can save your skin number six upgrade  your spell's and higgledy z' unlike  weapons and armor you won't find new  spells in the wild instead you will need  to visit the evermore spell works here  you can level up your current spells and  learn new ones  unfortunately leveling up and unlocking  new spells will cost you money and  resources so choose wisely higgledy s on  the other hand can be found in the wild  hiding in stones like these if you have  the correct item you can lure them out  but if not you can brew new ones at the  hIgG Lurie you want to return to the  Hitler II often to nurture your higgledy  's they max out at level 10 and can  prove useful near the end of the game  number 7 check back often your Kingdom  will earn money and resources as you  play but your coffers can only hold so  much money coffer upgrades should be a  high priority but in order to maximize  your profit and resources you'll want to  return often to collect your kingly  taxes the same goes for research  projects in order for research projects  to take effect you must return to your  kingdom and hit complete research to  make the most of your time try to have  as many research projects going as  possible  although ninokuni isn't overly complex  there are a lot of systems at play here  and if you ignore one you could put  yourself at a considerable disadvantage  if you have any more tips drop them in  the comments below and if you have any  questions feel free to reach out to me  on Twitter thanks for watching  [Music]
 

